    "updated_at": "2019-09-11T05:53:01Z",
    "body": "Huh, I didn't even think that that would be possible. I specifically set the PKGBUILD supported architectures to `x86_64` only because we haven't been able to do cross-platform testing yet.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, I think we'll need to rework our test suites a little bit before we're confident enough to release official ARM builds (or at least, I wouldn't be comfortable releasing them the way our tests work right now), so we won't have this available very soon.\r\n\r\nIf you'd like to upgrade `starship` and you don't want to go through a recompile process, I think you can use `cross` to do a cross-platform build. Follow the [instructions](https://github.com/rust-embedded/cross#installation) to get cross set up and ready (make sure to start the docker container). Then just clone the repository (or download a copy of the source code), and do\r\n\r\n```\r\ncross build --release --target arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat should put a binary at `target/arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf/release/starship` that you can copy over to your RPi and move to the correct directory.\r\n\r\nAgain, the reason we're not doing this ourselves is because we don't have the ability to test these binaries, so you're definitely wandering into \"unsupported\" territory here, but you can try this if you'd like to stay up to date while we get those tests sorted out.",
