    "body": "initial build and init'l  testing , i packed rpms , and initial ebuild has been sourced to rust by gentoo-devs. \r\n**\"kick the tires\" from build dir,**  on RPI4 Gentoo install. \r\n**POC/proof of work basically..** \r\n\r\n```\r\npi64 ~/starship/target/release # uname -a\r\nLinux pi64 5.4.45-v8-3b41649ff96d-p4-bis+ #2 SMP PREEMPT Tue Jun 16 14:11:43 GMT 2020 aarch64 GNU/Linux\r\n``` \r\n**host proof.** \r\n\r\noh-my-bash/zsh  supposed to clean up shell but make path's hidden etc.. add plugins ,, but meh...  \r\nthis looks more on the fly fun and configurable long term that is. \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/issues/1431  top is a snapshot of build dir with cargo build on aarch64 \r\n\r\nbottom cargo deb/cargo rpm , dose cargo build > deb > rpm respectively \r\n\r\nspecs and Debian goodies to bake debs/rpms ie via docker in x86/amd64/arm64/Borg-cube-os/etc \r\nwhat ever fills your airlock , n docker containers ... \r\ncargo deb/n cargo rpm , [cargo ebuild](https://packages.gentoo.org/packages/dev-util/cargo-ebuild) [cargo arch](https://crates.io/crates/cargo-arch) \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/gentoo/gentoo-rust/blob/master/app-shells/starship/starship-0.42.0.ebuild  pending Manifest for crates. \r\ntypicall ebuilds in rust often quite cross-plafrom \r\n\r\ni can say with a RPi4 or Rock64pro , these will build .. aarch64\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
